{
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "start": 3.5,
   "end": 8.236,
   "text": "I run the projector at an old drive-in, out past the edge of town."
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "start": 8.836,
   "end": 16.964,
   "text": "The owner had one rule. If a car stays in the back row after the last movie... don't walk over to it. Just shut down, and go home."
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "start": 17.564,
   "end": 20.999,
   "text": "For three summers, every car left on time."
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "start": 21.599,
   "end": 26.868,
   "text": "Then, on closing night, one stayed. Back row. Engine off. Windows fogged white."
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "start": 27.668,
   "end": 31.316,
   "text": "I shut off the projector. The big screen went black."
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "start": 32.216,
   "end": 34.264,
   "text": "Then it flickered back on."
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "start": 36.464,
   "end": 42.608,
   "text": "There was no film in the machine. But the screen was showing the parking lot... filmed from that back row."
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "start": 43.308,
   "end": 47.255,
   "text": "Nothing moved. Just moths, circling the speaker poles."
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "start": 48.755,
   "end": 55.837,
   "text": "Then, on the screen, my booth door opened. And I watched myself walk out... across the gravel... toward that car."
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "start": 56.637,
   "end": 60.243,
   "text": "But I hadn't moved. My hand was still on the switch."
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "start": 61.043,
   "end": 65.608,
   "text": "On the screen, I climbed into that car... and everything went black."
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "start": 67.408,
   "end": 73.488,
   "text": "I locked the booth until sunrise. At dawn, the car was gone. I went down to drive home."
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "start": 74.588,
   "end": 82.887,
   "text": "My car wasn't where I'd parked it. It was in the back row now... windows fogged white. And someone in the driver's seat... was waving at me."
  }
 ],
